y_i is the requested transformation, \rho_i is interpretive residue, and \tau_i is provenance: reader, basis, context, operator, reference, order, and time.

Hammer the residue into:

\rho_i=
(P,A,L,X,E,U)

for preserved, added, lost, transformed, emergent, unexplained information.

Honey is selected residue:

H=\mathcal S(\rho_1,\ldots,\rho_n)

but selection must reward more than repetition. A useful conceptual fitness is

F_H
\propto
\frac{
\text{novelty}\,
\text{utility}\,
\text{cross-basis survival}\,
\text{reality support}\,
\text{independence}
